{"unit_slug":"eldritch_blast","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","attack_roll","damage","on_hit_window","spell_root","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","opens_window","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"attack_roll_phase.count","justification":"Eldritch Blast's cantrip upgrade fires N separate attack rolls per cast, where N scales by character level (1@L1-4, 2@L5-10, 3@L11-16, 4@L17+). The current 'attack_roll' ActivationPhase has no 'count' field — it is always exactly one attack roll per phase entry. Adding an optional 'count: ThresholdTiers<number>' with axis='character' to the attack_roll phase variant would express this directly and cleanly.","evidence":"The spell creates two beams at level 5, three beams at level 11, and four beams at level 17. You can direct the beams at the same target or at different ones. Make a separate attack roll for each beam."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Attachment.target.selection: mode 'repeated'","justification":"Alternatively, the TargetSelection union needs a 'repeated' mode (as distinct from 'choose_up_to') to express 'N independent attack roll instances, each against any target in range, where N is a character-level threshold-tiered count'. The existing 'choose_up_to' with SlotScaling only handles slot-level linear multi-target selection for a single resolution, not N separate resolutions.","evidence":"Make a separate attack roll for each beam. [beams = 2 at L5, 3 at L11, 4 at L17]"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.825}
